{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BB9qv6CcHX9F3awq7gi1o9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# WI-281 — smoke tier true to its name: ≤ 60 s commit bar + a declared runtime budget\n2\t\n3\t**WI:** WI-281 · **Status:** queued · **Delivers:** the meta commit bar\n4\t(tests/conftest.py WI-122 tiering + the declared bar in status.md); no spine SR\n5\t— test-harness layer, 150-row empty-`SR-Refs` precedent.\n6\t\n7\t## Problem\n8\t\n9\tThe smoke tier is not a smoke test. Tiering is **opt-OUT** (WI-122,\n10\t`tests/conftest.py::SLOW_MODULES`): every collected test is `smoke` unless its\n11\tmodule is one of 15 named heavy end-to-end modules — so the commit bar runs\n12\t**1088 of 1378 tests (79%)**. Measured on the dev box (2026-07-23, 3.11.9 venv,\n13\t`-n auto`, three runs): **6:12 / 6:51 / 8:01 wall** — against a declared\n14\t\"~3.3 min\" in status.md that was already generous. The owner's directive\n15\t(2026-07-23): a smoke test answers *\"is it basically alive?\"* — the per-commit\n16\tbar should run in **≤ 60 seconds**, and the runtime should be **its own\n17\tdeclared budget item** so drift is caught, not re-discovered.\n18\t\n19\tWhy it matters: the bar's cost shapes behavior. Sessions pay it on every\n20\tcommit (the session-protocol §3 commit bar), so a 7-minute \"smoke\" either slows\n21\tevery loop iteration or tempts skipping the bar — both worse than a fast bar\n22\tplus the unchanged full suite at slice/phase close and in CI.\n23\t\n24\tThe WI-122 intent worth preserving: opt-out means a NEW test lands in the\n25\tcommit bar by default (\"never a false green\" by omission), and `smoke`/`slow`\n26\t**partition** the suite (`test_smoke_tier.py` guards it). The intent worth\n27\tcorrecting: at 1378 tests the generous default has inverted the tier's\n28\tpurpose.\n29\t\n30\t## Approach\n31\t\n32\tTwo deliverables — the re-tier and the budget sensor. Measure first, then cut:\n33\t\n34\t- **(a) Measure.** One `-m smoke --durations=0` run (plus per-module wall\n35\t  totals); record the module-level ranking in the close deliverable. Expected\n36\t  shape: the cost concentrates in modules driving subprocesses / bootstrapped\n37\t  scaffolds through `conftest.run_py` (subprocess-coverage overhead included) —\n38\t  the same class the existing 15 SLOW_MODULES already name.\n39\t- **(b) Re-tier to the budget.** Preferred: **keep the opt-out partition**\n40\t  (new tests still default into the bar) but move whole modules to `slow` by\n41\t  the measured ranking until smoke fits ≤ 60 s with headroom (~45 s target),\n42\t  drawing the line at the mechanical boundary where possible (subprocess/\n43\t  scaffold modules out; in-process unit modules in). Fallback if the budget\n44\t  cannot hold that way: flip to the **opt-IN `@smoke` posture the kit itself\n45\t  ships** (`project-trajectory/pytest.ini` uses opt-in marks with unmarked =\n46\t  full-suite-only — the meta-repo would then match its own template; note the\n47\t  erosion risk: new tests default OUT of the bar). Record whichever line is\n48\t  drawn and why in the spec/close notes.\n49\t- **(c) The budget item.** Declare the budget once and give it a sensor that\n50\t  bites, in the repo's growth-sensor idiom (`test_module_size_ratchet.py`,\n51\t  `test_dashboard_size_budget.py`):\n52\t  - **Declared home:** a `smoke-budget` entry alongside the tier declaration\n53\t    (docs/stack.ini `[tiers]` vicinity) — seconds for humans/CI, plus the\n54\t    deterministic proxy below.\n55\t  - **Deterministic sensor (always-on):** wall-clock asserts are\n56\t    machine-dependent and flaky, so the *ratchet* budgets what is\n57\t    deterministic — smoke-tier **membership** (collected-count ceiling, and/or\n58\t    the SLOW_MODULES line itself). Exceeding it fails the suite with the\n59\t    \"raise deliberately or re-tier\" message the size ratchets use.\n60\t  - **Wall-clock check (where timing is stable):** CI times the smoke step\n61\t    against the declared seconds budget (warn locally, enforce in CI — the\n62\t    build session picks warn-vs-fail per lane and records it).\n63\t- **(d) Update the declared surfaces** that state the bar's cost/shape:\n64\t  status.md \"Bar (per commit)\" (~3.3 min text), the `pytest.ini` header\n65\t  comment, `tests/conftest.py`'s WI-122 block, and the `session-protocol`\n66\t  skill §3 if it names the runtime. `test_smoke_tier.py`'s partition guard\n67\t  stays green throughout.\n68\t\n69\t**Hard edges:** no test is deleted or weakened — re-tiered only; the full\n70\tsuite (`-q -n auto`, slice/phase close + CI) is untouched; `smoke`+`slow`\n71\tremain a total partition.\n72\t\n73\t## Interfaces\n74\t\n75\tNo cross-module seam — acts only within `tests/` (conftest tiering, the new\n76\tbudget sensor, `test_smoke_tier.py`), `pytest.ini`, and the declared-bar prose\n77\thomes (docs/status.md, docs/stack.ini comment vicinity, the session-protocol\n78\tskill). Intra-module, test/harness layer. Nearest seam for reference: SR-007's\n79\tdeclared stack profile (`docs/stack.ini [tiers]` is already the tier\n80\tdeclaration check.py reads), unchanged in shape.\n81\t\n82\t## Done-when\n83\t\n84\t- [ ] Measured module ranking recorded; the re-tiered smoke runs **≤ 60 s**\n85\t      wall at `-n auto` on the dev box (real output pasted; ~45 s target for\n86\t      headroom).\n87\t- [ ] `smoke`/`slow` still partition the suite (`test_smoke_tier.py` green);\n88\t      no test deleted; full suite count unchanged.\n89\t- [ ] The budget item exists: declared value + deterministic membership\n90\t      ratchet that **bites** (mutating the tier past the ceiling fails), and\n91\t      the CI wall-clock check wired with its warn/fail choice recorded.\n92\t- [ ] Declared surfaces updated (status.md bar text, pytest.ini header,\n93\t      conftest WI-122 block, session-protocol §3 if it names the runtime).\n94\t- [ ] Commit bar green — run with the NEW tier (`pytest -q -n auto -m smoke`\n95\t      + `check_docs.py`) plus one full-suite run proving nothing was lost.\n96\t- [ ] Row set `done` (Deliverable filled, SpecRef cleared); spec archived to\n97\t      `docs/archive/specs/` with close date.\n98\t\n99\t## Notes / open questions\n100\t\n101\t- Filed 2026-07-23 (owner directive: \"a smoke test is supposed to be just\n102\t  that\"). **Re-fronted the same day (owner ruling): `Priority=1`** — the id\n103\t  tie-break keeps WI-275 first, this WI second, so every subsequent session's\n104\t  commit bar runs against the tightened tier.\n105\t- The 79% smoke share means the bar currently *re-runs most of the full suite*\n106\t  per commit — the cut is large by construction; expect smoke to land in the\n107\t  low hundreds of tests. Anything cut still runs at slice/phase close + CI.\n108\t- If the dev box's `-n auto` worker count materially differs from CI's, the\n109\t  seconds budget is per-lane; the deterministic membership ratchet is the\n110\t  shared floor — this is why the budget item is split in two.\n111\t\n112\t## Measured ranking & re-tier decision (WI-281 close)\n113\t\n114\t**Measurement (dev box, 2026-07-23, 3.11.9 venv, `-n auto`, 24 cores).** The\n115\tpre-change smoke tier: **1088/1378 tests, 351 s wall** (`5:51`; matches the\n116\tspec's 6–8 min band). Per-module wall totals (setup+call+teardown summed across\n117\tthe tier, `--durations=0`) rank the cost — and it concentrates exactly where the\n118\tspec predicted, in the modules driving subprocesses/scaffolds through\n119\t`conftest.run_py`:\n120\t\n121\t| module (moved to `slow`) | tier-wall s | module (moved to `slow`) | tier-wall s |\n122\t|---|---:|---|---:|\n123\t| test_gen_trajectory | 440.8 | test_modules_registry | 43.1 |\n124\t| test_agent_loop_review | 179.5 | test_agent_loop_worker | 41.1 |\n125\t| test_agent_loop | 170.5 | test_ac_advisory | 34.8 |\n126\t| test_trace | 166.8 | test_check_stubs | 26.7 |\n127\t| test_check_docs | 124.4 | test_perf_budgets | 25.2 |\n128\t| test_registry_checks | 96.2 | test_procurement | 20.4 |\n129\t| test_check_privacy | 87.4 | test_gen_release_checklist | 17.8 |\n130\t| test_agent_loop_critique | 87.2 | test_assets | 16.5 |\n131\t| test_check_harness | 79.3 | test_gen_arch_map | 13.0 |\n132\t| test_trajectory | 60.5 | test_trace_golden | 12.6 |\n133\t| test_components_registry | 58.4 | test_gate_policy | 11.2 |\n134\t| test_derive_gate | 53.7 | test_run_menu | 11.0 |\n135\t| test_gen_okf | 51.5 | test_agent_loop_env | 9.1 |\n136\t| test_gen_trajectory_pending | 44.0 | | |\n137\t\n138\t**Line drawn — the MECHANICAL boundary (preferred approach, not the opt-IN\n139\tfallback).** The opt-out partition is KEPT (a new in-process test still defaults\n140\tinto the bar — the WI-122 \"never a false green by omission\" intent). The 27\n141\tmodules above joined the 15 existing `SLOW_MODULES` (→ 42) on one rule:\n142\t*cost dominated by driving the heavy scripts (gen_trajectory / trace / check\\* /\n143\tagent_loop) or bootstrapping a scaffold as subprocesses → runs at close + CI, not\n144\tper commit*. The retained smoke set is the in-process unit modules (decision /\n145\trouting / schedule / planning / registry-parse / dogfood-sync / the size &\n146\tbudget ratchets). No test deleted or weakened; `smoke`+`slow` stay a total\n147\tpartition (`test_smoke_tier.py`); the full suite is untouched. The opt-IN\n148\tfallback was **not** needed (the budget held with the opt-out posture intact).\n149\t\n150\t**Result:** re-tiered smoke = **360 tests → 7.29 s wall** (now 366 tests with the\n151\t6 new budget/tier tests — 2 in `test_smoke_budget.py` + 4 in\n152\t`test_check_smoke_budget.py`; still ~7 s, re-measured 7.02 s this session), well\n153\tunder the 60 s bar and the ~45 s headroom target.\n154\t\n155\t**Budget item (split in two, per the spec).**\n156\t- *Declared home:* `docs/stack.ini [smoke-budget]` — `seconds = 60` (per-lane\n157\t  wall target) + `max-tests = 450` (the deterministic proxy, ~23% headroom over\n158\t  366 for in-process growth).\n159\t- *Deterministic sensor (always-on, GATES):* `tests/test_smoke_budget.py`\n160\t  independently collects `-m smoke` and asserts the count ≤ `max-tests`.\n161\t  **Bite-proven live:** with the ceiling temporarily set to 300 the real count\n162\t  (366) failed with the \"re-tier or re-stamp\" message; re-adding any one big\n163\t  slowed module (test_agent_loop ~113, test_gen_trajectory ~98, test_trajectory\n164\t  ~115) blows past 450.\n165\t- *Wall-clock check (CI, WARNS):* `scripts/check_smoke_budget.py` times the\n166\t  declared smoke command against `seconds`; wired into `.github/workflows/test.yml`\n167\t  as a one-lane `smoke-budget` job. **Warn/fail choice = WARN**, recorded here:\n168\t  GitHub-hosted runners have far fewer cores than the 24-core dev box the 60 s\n169\t  target was set on, so a hard time-assert would be flaky — this follows the\n170\t  repo's warn-first stance for noisy runtime metrics (perf budgets `Gate=warn`);\n171\t  the deterministic ratchet is the enforced shared floor. A stable lane can pick\n172\t  `--mode enforce`.\n173\t\n174\t**Deviations / carry-overs.**\n175\t- **status.md bar text NOT updated here.** Done-when (d) lists `docs/status.md`\n176\t  \"Bar (per commit)\" (`~3.3 min`), but the parallel-dispatch worker contract\n177\t  bars editing root coordination truth (`docs/status.md`) on a train branch —\n178\t  the integrator/owner must update that prose to the ≤ 60 s / ~7 s re-tier at\n179\t  integration. The other declared surfaces WERE updated: `pytest.ini` header +\n180\t  markers, `tests/conftest.py` WI-122 block, the `session-protocol` skill §3\n181\t  (all three materialized copies kept byte-identical).\n182\t- **One pre-existing Windows red remains in smoke:**\n183\t  `test_session_stdin.py::test_run_session_codex_reads_last_message_not_transcript`\n184\t  — a retained in-process module. This is **WI-275's** subject (the two known\n185\t  Windows shim-refusal reds), not this WI's