ns a NEW test lands in the\ncommit bar by default (\"never a false green\" by omission), and `smoke`/`slow`\n**partition** the suite (`test_smoke_tier.py` guards it). The intent worth\ncorrecting: at 1378 tests the generous default has inverted the tier's\npurpose.\n\n## Approach\n\nTwo deliverables — the re-tier and the budget sensor. Measure first, then cut:\n\n- **(a) Measure.** One `-m smoke --durations=0` run (plus per-module wall\n  totals); record the module-level ranking in the close deliverable. Expected\n  shape: the cost concentrates in modules driving subprocesses / bootstrapped\n  scaffolds through `conftest.run_py` (subprocess-coverage overhead included) —\n  the same class the existing 15 SLOW_MODULES already name.\n- **(b) Re-tier to the budget.** Preferred: **keep the opt-out partition**\n  (new tests still default into the bar) but move whole modules to `slow` by\n  the measured ranking until smoke fits ≤ 60 s with headroom (~45 s target),\n  drawing the line at the mechanical boundary where possible (subprocess/\n  scaffold modules out; in-process unit modules in). Fallback if the budget\n  cannot hold that way: flip to the **opt-IN `@smoke` posture the kit itself\n  ships** (`project-trajectory/pytest.ini` uses opt-in marks with unmarked =\n  full-suite-only — the meta-repo would then match its own template; note the\n  erosion risk: new tests default OUT of the bar). Record whichever line is\n  drawn and why in the spec/close notes.\n- **(c) The budget item.** Declare the budget once and give it a sensor that\n  bites, in the repo's growth-sensor idiom (`test_module_size_ratchet.py`,\n  `test_dashboard_size_budget.py`):\n  - **Declared home:** a `smoke-budget` entry alongside the tier declaration\n    (docs/stack.ini `[tiers]` vicinity) — seconds for humans/CI, plus the\n    deterministic proxy below.\n  - **Deterministic sensor (always-on):** wall-clock asserts are\n    machine-dependent and flaky, so the *ratchet* budgets what is\n    deterministic — smoke-tier **membership** (collected-count ceiling, and/or\n    the SLOW_MODULES line itself). Exceeding it fails the suite with the\n    \"raise deliberately or re-tier\" message the size ratchets use.\n  - **Wall-clock check (where timing is stable):** CI times the smoke step\n    a
