{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdJjhbvi9e78tNY5jwbYR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four review-A findings are resolved or correctly routed, the commit is in with the required trailers, and the tree is clean.\n\n## Summary — WI-281 rework (review A: CHANGES-REQUESTED, 4 findings)\n\nCommit `d8d50e6` on `llm/train/p0-g3-WI-281-9ae9`. Two findings fixed in scope; two are integrator/owner close-out that the parallel-dispatch worker contract bars a train-branch worker from touching.\n\n**Finding 1 — Windows smoke red (FIXED).** The re-tier had left `test_session_stdin` in the commit bar, and its `codex_reads_last_message` test fails on Windows: `run_session`'s batch-shim guard refuses a `.cmd` launcher that carries *no* `{prompt}` at all — a real guard bug that is **WI-275's** open subject (it fails identically on the integration base), not fixable from this re-tiering WI. I took the reviewer's named in-scope alternative and re-tiered the whole module (a `run_session` subprocess/shim-transport module that hosts those reds) into `conftest.SLOW_MODULES`, module-granular like every entry. Commit bar is now green on every supported OS — `-m smoke -n auto` → **349 passed** (was 365 passed / 1 failed). No test deleted or weakened; the module still runs at close + CI.\n\n**Finding 2 — CI wall-clock ran `--mode warn` (FIXED).** The `smoke-budget` lane now runs `--mode enforce` (exit 1 on breach). The build session chose warn fearing flakiness on fewer-core runners; I re-measured across worker counts and disproved it — the re-tiered tier is startup-dominated, not core-bound: **~7.5s/24, ~8.1s/4, ~10.5s/2 cores**, so the 60s budget keeps ~5× headroom and enforce is safe. warn→enforce *strengthens* the gate (not a weakening), so no spec-change approval was needed. The deterministic membership ratchet stays the machine-independent floor in the main test job.\n\n**Findings 3 & 4 — status.md `~3.3 min` prose / row-close + spec-archive (DEFERRED to integrator/owner).** Both are root-coordination-truth edits the worker contract explicitly bars on a train branch (`agent_loop.py` NEVER-edit list; SR-060). `docs/status.md` and the WI row's Status/Deliverable are the integrator's `_rewrite_wi_rows`/status-regen at integration — a worker flipping them (or archiving the spec while `SpecRef` is still live and the row still `queued`) would strand coordination state. Both reviewer findings carry the `→ @owner` route, consistent with this split. I documented all four dispositions in a **Review A rework** section in `docs/specs/WI-281.md`.\n\n**Verification (3.11.9 venv, 24 cores):**\n- Commit bar green: smoke 349 passed (7.48s, Windows); check_docs 0 broken; ruff format+lint clean; real enforce check 8.3s within 60s.\n- Full suite unchanged — **1377 passed, 5 skipped, 2 failed** (6:54): the 2 failures are the known WI-275 Windows batch-shim reds, **both now in the slow tier** (off the commit bar, on at close + CI). Nothing lost.\n- Pre-commit gate battery all PASS (skills-sync 12/12 in sync, derived-gate G3, registry-integrity 0/0, arch-map, trajectory).\n\nFiles: `tests/conftest.py`, `.github/workflows/test.yml`, `scripts/check_smoke_budget.py`, `docs/stack.ini`, `pytest.ini`, `docs/specs/WI-281.md`, and the 3 byte-identical `session-protocol/SKILL.md` copies (+113/−55).\n\nOne advisory carry-over for the integrator: `check_trajectory` WARNs that WI-281's SpecRef changed after its row was last touched — resolved by touching/closing the row at integration (a worker-barred edit)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":88,"cache_read_input_tokens":181775,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":88},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"42df3